      <div type="clause" n="29.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 29.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 29.3" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="563" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="l" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.l"/> ad comitatum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.30"/> secundum legem submonitus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.17"/> uenire noluerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.31"/>, XX ma[n]c.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="m" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.m"/> culpa sit in Westsexa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.32"/>, et — si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.33"/> de<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="n" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.n"/> nominatis placitis inplacitatus non erat — termino<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.34"/> congruo cause sue prosequende facultatem habeat.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 563 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.l" n="l" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Verklagter</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The defendant</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.m" n="m" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mͣ <hi rend="italic">Sc;</hi> marc. <hi rend="italic">übrige; gebessert aus</hi> 53, 1, <hi rend="italic">wo dies wiederholt und Quelle deutlich wird:</hi> oferhyrnesse = 120 <hi rend="italic">Schil.</hi> = 20 <hi rend="italic">Manc.; vgl.</hi> 34, 3. 35, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mͣ Sc; marc. the rest; corrected from 53, 1, where this is repeated and the source becomes clear: oferhyrnesse = 120 shill. = 20 manc.; cf. 34, 3. 35, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.n" n="n" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in bestimmt bezeichnete Anklage versetzt: <hi rend="italic">der Fall von</hi> 29, 3<hi rend="italic">a; vgl.</hi> 46, 1. 50</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">placed under a specifically named charge: the case of 29, 3<hi rend="italic">a</hi>; cf. 46, 1. 50</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">summo. <hi rend="italic">stets Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">summo. Lond throughout</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hundredum <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hundredum Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-int <hi rend="italic">Wh</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-int Wh</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wetse. <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Wetse. Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">563</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vom Corr. über</hi> testimonio <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">by the corrector above testimonio Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_29-3.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Vorladung 13. Die Hervorhebung von Wessex hier und öfter bezeichnet den Enstehungsort von Hn; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. Einl. 6.—Nicht wie hier Beklagte, sondern kraft Besitzes bestimmter Länderei zur Gerichtsfolge beim Grafschaftstage in Kent Pflichtige <hi rend="italic">si fuerint præmoniti ut conveniant ad sciram, et si non venerint, de hac forisfactura rex C sol. habebit</hi>; Weistum von Pennenden Heath (<hi rend="italic">o</hi>. zu 23, 1{b}). Die Stelle ist also nicht heranzuziehen.—<hi rend="italic">Qui ad hundretum</hi>{30} <hi rend="italic">s</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">XX mancas</hi> richtig, wie ich besserte—29, 3a <hi rend="italic">placitis</hi>{35} Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Vorladung 13. The emphasis on Wessex here and frequently elsewhere indicates the place where Hn originated; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 6. — Not defendants, as here, but persons bound by virtue of holding particular lands to do suit at the shire court in Kent are meant in <hi rend="italic">si fuerint præmoniti ut conveniant ad sciram, et si non venerint, de hac forisfactura rex C sol. habebit</hi>; declaration of Pennenden Heath (<hi rend="italic">above</hi> on 23, 1{b}). The passage is therefore not to be adduced. — <hi rend="italic">Qui ad hundretum</hi>{30} <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. — <hi rend="italic">XX mancas</hi> correct, as I emended — 29, 3a <hi rend="italic">placitis</hi>{35} Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
